\section{Process overview}
The report separates inputs, analysis and recommendations to make its conclusions traceable.
\begin{figure}[H]\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}[node distance=9mm]
\node[ofinbox] (a) {Source material};
\node[ofinbox,right=of a] (b) {Analysis and checks};
\node[ofinbox,right=of b] (c) {Report and findings};
\draw[ofinflow] (a)--(b);\draw[ofinflow] (b)--(c);
\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Illustrative report production process.}
\end{figure}
\section{Delivery comparison}
\begin{table}[H]\centering
\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{lXr}\toprule
\rowcolor{OfinTint}\textbf{Period} & \textbf{Observation} & \textbf{Completed tasks}\\\midrule
January & Baseline for this synthetic series & 12\\
February & Additional capacity in the example & 18\\
March & Highest volume in the supplied example & 24\\\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\caption{Illustrative values supplied solely for template verification.}
\end{table}
\newpage
\section{Quantitative view}
\begin{figure}[H]\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[ybar,bar width=15pt,ymin=0,ymax=30,symbolic x coords={Jan,Feb,Mar},xtick=data,xlabel={Period},ylabel={Completed tasks}]
\addplot[fill=OfinNavy,draw=OfinNavy] coordinates {(Jan,12)(Feb,18)(Mar,24)};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Synthetic task volumes; source: the illustrative values in Table 1.}
\end{figure}
\subsection{Interpretation}
The final illustrative value is twice the baseline: $(24-12)/12=100\%$. This is an arithmetic demonstration, not a business forecast.
\section{Recommendations}
\begin{enumerate}\item Validate source figures before drawing operational conclusions.\item Compare consistent time periods and state measurement definitions.\item Use a table for exact values and a plot when the pattern matters.\end{enumerate}
